{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_ovyb2mlmjaqudfi35twimy6rojweldglswqldvy47lcwx6k5dodq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete — all four phases pass.\n\n## Completion gate\n\n| Gate | Status |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md`: 0 missing/undefined non-libc symbols | ✅ symbol diff **empty both directions**; `ldd -r` clean |\n| Phase B: every `CONFIGS.md` row passes randomized inputs | ✅ 45/45 rows |\n| Binary stdout comparison | ✅ vacuous — no `add_executable`, no `[[bin]]`/`main.rs`. Library stdout compared byte-for-byte via fd-1 capture instead |\n| Phase C: every `ERRORS.md` row has a passing test | ✅ 29/29 numbered rows (+ row 17a documented UB) |\n| Holds under every feature combination | ✅ 12/12 configurations, 82 tests each |\n\n`Cargo.toml` has no `[features]`, so I widened the matrix on the axes that *do* exist: 2 feature invocations × 2 Rust profiles (release/**debug**) × 3 C builds (`-O0`/`-O2`/CMake default).\n\n## Two real bugs found and fixed\n\n**1. `copy_data_block` aborted on an aliased call.** The Rust used `core::ptr::copy_nonoverlapping`; its `debug_assertions` precondition check **aborts the process** (SIGABRT) on `copy_data_block(p, p)`, while the C's `memcpy` returns normally. Only visible against a debug-profile `.so`. Now reads the 40 bytes into a temporary before storing — reproducing glibc's load-then-store `memcpy` for all aliased and disjoint inputs.\n\n**2. The C has no stable behaviour for *partially* overlapping copies.** Testing revealed the C library disagreeing with **itself**: at `-O0` GCC calls glibc `memcpy` (overlap-safe), at `-O2` it inlines a forward load/store sequence whose stores clobber later loads. No Rust behaviour can match \"the C\" here, so it's documented as `ERRORS.md` row 17a rather than asserted. This is why the runner builds the C three ways.\n\n## Notes\n\n- `cargo check` was already clean; no compile errors existed.\n- Cargo couldn't reach crates.io through the proxy, so I pinned `libloading 0.8.9` + `cfg-if 1.0.4` (both already in the local registry cache) in `Cargo.lock` and build with `--offline`.\n- The suite **must** run single-threaded — it redirects the process-global fd 1, and libtest's own parallel progress writes otherwise land inside a capture window. The harness detects this and fails loudly with instructions rather than producing flaky mismatches (I hit exactly this false positive first).\n- Three of my own test expectations were wrong initially (fall-through deltas for `case 4`/`case 3`, a seed overflow). In each case the C was right and I corrected the test — `c_src/` is untouched (source timestamps unchanged; only the prescribed `build/` dir added).\n\nArtifacts: `translation/SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`, `run_all.sh`, and `tests/{common/mod.rs,phase_b_lowlevel.rs,phase_b_overunder.rs,phase_c_errors.rs,phase_d_symbols.rs,smoke.rs}`. Reproduce with `cd translation && ./run_all.sh`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2326,"cache_read_input_tokens":131354,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2326,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"29147586-8ff7-4fa7-b031-69a75ddbd65b","uuid":"a842b864-2c54-4ba0-a8b1-47eab6491412","timestamp":"2026-09-05T16:00:51.597Z"}
